## UI work — read the design rulebook first

<!-- Paste into your project's CLAUDE.md and fix the paths (design-kit/ → where the kit lives). -->

Before adding or changing anything visible (CSS, markup, UI copy, charts), read the section you need:

- values (type, colour, spacing, radius, motion, sizes) → `design-kit/docs/foundations.md`
- elements (buttons, fields, lists, cards, menus, alerts, empty states…) → `design-kit/docs/components.md`
- page layouts, states, confirm/undo, forms, responsive → `design-kit/docs/patterns.md`
- graphs and charts → `design-kit/docs/data-viz.md`
- any user-facing text → `design-kit/docs/writing.md`
- project-specific choices that override the kit → `design-kit/docs/decisions.md`

Rules that apply to every change:

- Target feel: a native macOS / iOS app. Desktop follows the macOS HIG (body 13, controls 28); phones (≤760px) the iOS
  HIG at the "Small" Dynamic Type size (body 15), with a bottom tab bar.
- Only tokens from `design-kit/tokens.css`: `--t-*` for type, semantic colours (`--label`, `--fill-*`, `--accent`…),
  `--s-*` spacing, `--r-*` radii. No px font sizes, hex/rgb colours or ad-hoc radii in page CSS or inline styles.
  Inline `style=` only for data colours (via a `--c` variable) and dynamic sizes (bar widths).
- Use the `ui-*` components from `design-kit/components.css`. Component selectors are `:where([data-ui]) .ui-x` and the
  kit loads first, so page CSS only arranges them (grid, width, spacing) with single classes — no `!important`.
  A component that isn't in components.md gets added to `design-kit/specimen.html` and to the doc first.
- States use `aria-pressed` / `aria-current`, not an `.on` class.
- One accent colour for primary buttons, selection and links. No tinted grey surfaces; inside a card, separate items
  with 0.5px separators instead of grey boxes.
- Confirmations use `AppUI.confirm`, focused tasks `AppUI.sheet`, results `AppUI.toast` — never `confirm()`/`prompt()`.
- Copy: follow writing.md (Korean: 해요체 sentences, noun labels, the glossary's terms, short action words
  저장·편집·삭제·제거·추가·완료·취소), all strings through the project's i18n.
- A rule you need to break or change → write it in `design-kit/docs/decisions.md` first.

After UI changes run the design lint (it must pass; it compares against a baseline):

```
python design-kit/design_lint.py
```

If you removed legacy values, lock it in with `python design-kit/design_lint.py --update`. Never run `--update` to make
new violations pass.
